{"step_index":1053,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:55:03Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-24T19:55:03-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-24T19:55:04-04:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\nEngine: Paschalion -> [GREGORIAN]\r\nEngine Init: Logic=[royal_doors] | Internal Content=[json_db/stamford]\r\nEngine: Loaded 447 assets from .\\assets\\stamford\r\nEngine: Loaded pre-computed almanac for year 2026 (annual_almanac_royal_doors_2026.json)\r\n# TYPICON: WEDNESDAY, JANUARY 14th, 2026.\r\n\r\nVENERABLE FATHERS SLAIN IN SINAI AND RAITHU; APODOSIS OF THEOPHANY - TONE VI.  \r\nWednesday service.  \r\nVestment colour: Bright (White or gold).  \r\n\r\n## DAILY VESPERS\r\n\r\nNo kathisma is appointed.  \r\n*At Lord, I Call�* we sing 6 Feast Stichera from the Menaion; Glory... Doxastikon of the Saint; Both now: Theotokion of the Feast.  \r\n<span class=\"rubric\">Daily Prokeimenon (Wednesday of the Octoechos), Tone V:</span> <span class=\"sung-text\">\"O Lord, save me by Your name, and in Your power be a judge for me\"</span>  \r\n<blockquote class=\"verse\"><span class=\"rubric\">Stichos:</span> <span class=\"sung-text\">O God, hear my prayer; listen to the words of my mouth.</span></blockquote>  \r\n**At the Aposticha:** We sing 3 daily Aposticha from the Octoechos; Glory, Both now: Aposticha Theotokion.  \r\n**At the Dismissal Troparia:** We sing the Troparion of the Feast; Glory, Both now: Theotokion.  \r\n\r\n## SMALL COMPLINE\r\n\r\nTroparia: Troparion of the Cross (first place, Wednesday/Friday), *\"O God of our fathers...\"* and the following three troparia.  \r\n\r\n## MIDNIGHT OFFICE\r\n\r\nMidnight Troparia: Troparion of the weekday, Troparion of the Saint (if any), daily Theotokion.  \r\n\r\n## DAILY MATINS\r\n\r\n*At The Lord is God�* we sing: Troparion of the feast, twice; Glory, Both now. Troparion of the feast, once.  \r\n\r\nWe read Kathismata 8, 9 and 10.  \r\n\r\nAfter the Kathismata (8, 9, and 10): We sing the Sessional Hymns from the Octoechos.  \r\n**Katavasia:** \"The depths\" (Tone II).  \r\nAt Ode IX, we sing the Magnification ('My soul magnifies the Lord...') and the refrains ('More honorable than the Cherubim...').  \r\n**At the Aposticha:** We sing 3 daily Aposticha from the Octoechos; Glory, Both now: Aposticha Theotokion.  \r\n**At the Dismissal Troparia:** We sing: Troparion of the Feast in Tone I; Glory, Both now: Troparion of the Feast.  \r\nDismissal Stavrotheotokion (Tone VI, Wednesday): Dismissal Theotokion for Wednesday in Tone VI.  \r\n\r\n## HOURS\r\n\r\n**At the Hours:** At all the hours: Troparion of the feast.  \r\nKontakia: at all the hours � Kontakion of the Venerable Fathers slain in Sinai and Raithu; Apodosis of Theophany.  \r\n\r\n## DIVINE LITURGY OF ST. JOHN CHRYSOSTOM\r\n\r\nPsalms of Typica; Beatitudes.  \r\n**Troparia and Kontakia:**  \r\nTroparion of the Feast.  \r\nKontakion of the Feast.  \r\n**Prokeimenon:**  \r\n> of the day (Tone V)\r\n**Epistle:**  \r\n> Weekday\r\n**Alleluia:**  \r\n> sung in Tone V.\r\n**Gospel:**  \r\n> Weekday\r\n**Communion Hymn:**  \r\n> \"I will take the cup of salvation, and I will call upon the name of the Lord.\"\r\n**Post-Communion Hymn:** \"We have seen the true light, we have received the heavenly Spirit...\"  \r\nDismissal: May Christ our true God...  \r\n\n"}
